For a POST or custom headers, pass an options object as the second argument [3]:

```ts
fetch('https://mywebsite.com/endpoint/', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    Accept: 'application/json',
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    firstParam: 'yourValue',
    secondParam: 'yourOtherValue',
  }),
});
```

React Native also includes `XMLHttpRequest`, so you can use it directly or use libraries built on it, such as axios or frisbee [4].

